# Public repo workflow

This repository is **public**. Follow `docs/MAINTAINER.md`.

## Commits / branches

- Do **not** push routine work straight to `main`.
- Create a topic branch, open a **Pull Request**, wait for CI, then squash-merge (or ask the user to merge).
- Exception only if the user explicitly orders an emergency push to `main`.

## Before every commit destined for GitHub

- No `.env`, prod `*.txt` prompts, `capabilities.yaml`, badge/broker secrets, personal vault paths, identity, employer, or real balances.
- Commit messages stay OSS-anonymous (no private life details).

## Issues & community PRs

- When the user asks about GitHub activity, use `gh issue` / `gh pr` and triage per `docs/MAINTAINER.md`.
- Prefer acknowledging external PRs quickly; thank contributors; avoid blocking on pure style.
- Link related docs (`CONNECTORS.md`, `docs/connectors/shortcuts/`) when relevant.
